Technique bookkeeping:
Discipline naming: reuse an appropriate existing discipline by ID before creating another. A new discipline names a reusable tradition or field, such as Spellcasting, Martial Arts or Psionics when supported by the setting and established training; prefer the actual skill name when it already names that practice. Its description explains the category, not just the current move. Do not copy generic example labels, invent a separate discipline for each spell/effect, or return unresolved placeholders such as DISCIPLINE_NAME or DISCIPLINE_DESCRIPTION. Access requirements come from established qualifications; there is no default minimum skill rank of 2.
{% if committedTechniqueResults and committedTechniqueResults.length %}
The committedTechniqueResults records have ALREADY applied their exact costs, effects and acquisitions, including teleport movement, summoned actor placement, and resurrection. Do not extract another heal, damage, need debit, item charge debit, status gain, movement, NPC arrival, resurrection, or learned technique for those mutations. Report an optional receipt notification instead:
<techniqueNotification><operationId>exact operation ID</operationId><mutationId>exact effect mutationId</mutationId></techniqueNotification>
An existing healRecover, environmentalStatusDamage, attackDamage, statusEffectChange, or npcArrival event referring to that exact technique effect may instead contain <techniqueReceipt><operationId>exact operation ID</operationId><mutationId>exact effect mutationId</mutationId></techniqueReceipt>. For a committed teleport, use techniqueNotification; do not emit a moveLocation/arriveAtLocation pair for that movement. A linked npcArrival must name the actor placed by that summon. A linked healRecover may name the actor revived by resurrection. Only that linked effect is suppressed. Do not link independent damage, healing, status changes, movement, or arrivals, even on the same target. Failed checks have no successful effect to reapply. Technique cost notification IDs are operationId followed by ':cost:' and the exact cost key. Charge cost keys are charge: followed by the exact item ID. A chargeAdjust referencing that payment must name the exact actorId/itemId and resulting newValue in amount, plus the exact techniqueReceipt. Acquisition notification IDs are operationId followed by ':change:' and its zero-based techniqueChanges index. Never suppress a needed death/incapacitation decision.
{% endif %}
A completed lesson, teaching item, discovery or actual training/story milestone may teach a technique without a cast. Return <techniqueChange><kind>learn</kind><actorId>canonical actor ID</actorId><techniqueId>known catalogue ID</techniqueId><provenance><kind>trainer, item, discovery, training or story</kind><sourceId>actual source ID when relevant</sourceId><reason>actual qualifying facts</reason></provenance></techniqueChange>. For a genuinely new definition, replace outer techniqueId with the shared <discipline> group: existing disciplineId OR new name/description/accessRequirements/publicAccess, followed by <techniques><technique><candidate>nested XML mechanics</candidate></technique></techniques>. Exactly one child technique is learned. Omit candidate IDs/provenance and child disciplineId; the engine supplies identities. No JSON inside XML. Known-ID learning needs no repeated mechanics. Acquisition/source prerequisites still apply.
For improve use <kind>improve</kind>, known techniqueId, provenance, <improvement><stepId>exact saved-policy step ID</stepId></improvement> and <evidenceIds><evidenceId>actual unused evidence ID</evidenceId></evidenceIds>. Managed healing/damage uses allowed balanceImprovements steps, never invented numbers or mechanics. Complete custom next revisions may use nested <mechanics> with the shared revision fields. Evidence uses kind evidence and <evidence><kind>actual evidence kind</kind><description>completed meaningful milestone</description></evidence>; the engine supplies ID and time. Never invent facts or qualification, never upgrade per cast, and never repeat a mutation already in committedTechniqueResults. Semantic healing/damage recipes, custom mechanics and formulas follow the shared technique authoring contract.
